Third-party OAuth client identity
---------------------------------

xAI account login ships a default OAuth client id:

    b1a00492-073a-47ea-816f-4c329264a828

This is the client id xAI publishes for the Grok CLI as a public desktop OAuth
client, registered against the loopback redirect http://127.0.0.1:56121/callback.
Codescribe uses it as the default so xAI sign-in works without the operator
registering an application; it is not a private registration and Codescribe does
not claim to be the Grok CLI.

An operator who registers their own xAI application overrides it in
Settings -> Keys (LLM_XAI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID) or via CODESCRIBE_XAI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID;
both are checked before this default.

No other provider ships a client id. OpenAI and Anthropic account login stays
gated on the operator supplying their own registration.
